  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Oracle Health Government Services has $1.3B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Oracle Health Government Services received 28 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $45.9M, and obligations are up 27.7% year over year. Oracle Health Government Services obligations have varied across recent fiscal years: FY21 $971M, FY22 $2B, FY23 $825M, FY24 $893M, FY25 $1B, and FY26 $1.3B. Oracle Health Government Services draws its FY2026 obligations primarily from the Department of Veterans Affairs, which obligated $1.3B. Oracle Health Government Services sells services classified under Computer Systems Design Services, which accounts for $1.3B of obligations in FY2026 to date. Oracle Health Government Services also shows obligations in Computer Facilities Management Services at $3.6M and Used Household and Office Goods Moving at $110K, while Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services shows $0 in obligations for the same period.",
